wlcs v1.8.1: the xdg-decoration tests that set a mode expect a decoration configure without the client ever committing.

set_mode_client_results_in_a_configure_event, set_mode_server_results_in_a_configure_event and
unset_mode_results_in_a_configure_event create a toplevel and its decoration, request a mode and wait for
zxdg_toplevel_decoration_v1.configure, but the surface is never committed. The decoration mode is part of the toplevel's
configure sequence ("the configured state should not be applied immediately. Clients must send an ack_configure in
response to this event"), and xdg-shell sends the first configure as the answer to the client's initial commit; Mir sends
one at once, which the protocol does not require. Same kind of defect as 0003's wm_capabilities_are_sent: the tests now
commit before they wait. Their expectation is unchanged: at least one decoration configure.

Applied by scripts/wlcs.sh with `git apply`; drop it when wlcs fixes the tests upstream.

diff --git a/tests/xdg_decoration_v1.cpp b/tests/xdg_decoration_v1.cpp
index 7e37095..8b64d7d 100644
--- a/tests/xdg_decoration_v1.cpp
+++ b/tests/xdg_decoration_v1.cpp
@@ -78,6 +78,10 @@ TEST_F(XdgDecorationV1Test, set_mode_client_results_in_a_configure_event)
 
     EXPECT_CALL(decoration, configure(_)).Times(AtLeast(1));
 
+    // The decoration mode travels with the toplevel's configure, and xdg-shell sends the first one as the answer to the
+    // client's initial commit. A client that never commits has asked for no configure (Mir sends one at once, which the
+    // protocol does not require).
+    wl_surface_commit(a_surface);
     a_client.roundtrip();
 }
 
@@ -90,6 +94,10 @@ TEST_F(XdgDecorationV1Test, set_mode_server_results_in_a_configure_event)
 
     EXPECT_CALL(decoration, configure(_)).Times(AtLeast(1));
 
+    // The decoration mode travels with the toplevel's configure, and xdg-shell sends the first one as the answer to the
+    // client's initial commit. A client that never commits has asked for no configure (Mir sends one at once, which the
+    // protocol does not require).
+    wl_surface_commit(a_surface);
     a_client.roundtrip();
 }
 
@@ -102,5 +110,9 @@ TEST_F(XdgDecorationV1Test, unset_mode_results_in_a_configure_event)
 
     EXPECT_CALL(decoration, configure(_)).Times(AtLeast(1));
 
+    // The decoration mode travels with the toplevel's configure, and xdg-shell sends the first one as the answer to the
+    // client's initial commit. A client that never commits has asked for no configure (Mir sends one at once, which the
+    // protocol does not require).
+    wl_surface_commit(a_surface);
     a_client.roundtrip();
 }
